; bfs.ent — breadth-first search over a deterministic graph (bench/SPEC.md)
; n from argv[1] (default 1000000). Edges: u -> (7u+3) mod n and
; u -> (13u+11) mod n for every u, plus u -> (u+1) mod n when u mod 3 = 0.
; Adjacency is a dict of per-node lists; dist is an int array (-1 =
; unreached); the frontier lives in a preallocated int-array queue (each node
; is enqueued at most once, so tail never passes n).
1000000 n!
has_args 'setn if
n@ dict adj!
n@ int array dist!
n@ int array q!
0 r! 0 s! 0 m!
0 n@ 'bld for
0 n@ 'negf for
dist@ 0 0 set
q@ 0 0 set
1 tail!
0 head!
'more 'step while
0 n@ 'tally for
"reached: " print r@ print
"unreached: " print n@ r@ sub print
"sum_dist: " print s@ print
"max_dist: " print m@ print
ret
setn: 1 arg_index n! ret
bld: u!
  u@ 7 mul 3 add n@ rem v1!
  u@ 13 mul 11 add n@ rem v2!
  list v1@ append v2@ append lst!
  u@ 3 rem 0 eq 'third 'put if_else
  ret
third: lst@ u@ 1 add n@ rem append lst! adj@ u@ lst@ set ret
put: adj@ u@ lst@ set ret
negf: i! dist@ i@ -1 set ret
more: head@ tail@ lt ret
step:
  q@ head@ get u!
  dist@ u@ get du!
  adj@ u@ get nb!
  head@ 1 add head!
  0 j!
  'vis_c 'vis_b while
  ret
vis_c: j@ nb@ length lt ret
vis_b:
  nb@ j@ get v!
  dist@ v@ get 0 lt 'visit 'vskip if_else
  j@ 1 add j!
  ret
visit:
  dist@ v@ du@ 1 add set
  q@ tail@ v@ set
  tail@ 1 add tail!
  ret
vskip: ret
tally: i!
  dist@ i@ get d!
  d@ 0 lt 'ts 'tc if_else
  ret
ts: ret
tc:
  r@ 1 add r!
  s@ d@ add s!
  d@ m@ gt 'tmax 'ts if_else
  ret
tmax: d@ m! ret
